---
/**
 * Upgrades `<al-theme>` — and ONLY `<al-theme>` — on every page of every site.
 *
 * WHY THIS EXISTS SEPARATELY FROM `LiveRuntime.astro`. That module imports the
 * whole element registry and is rendered only where a page mounts live
 * components, which is component detail pages and nothing else. Everywhere
 * else — every project's overview, foundations and component index — the
 * `<al-theme>` that Shell.astro wraps the shell in was never upgraded at all.
 *
 * That was invisible while the docs chrome was hardcoded neutral. It stopped
 * being invisible the moment the chrome moved onto `--al-theme-color-*`:
 * those custom properties are set by this element's `:host` rules, so a page
 * where it never upgrades renders the base bundle's values — i.e. the DEFAULT
 * brand's. Southleft's overview would have been Altitude grey while
 * Southleft's Button page was Southleft brown, on the same site.
 *
 * It is also what the boot blur waits on (`data-booting` in Shell.astro).
 * Without this, the pages with no live components would have had nothing to
 * wait for and would have stayed blurred for the length of the backstop.
 *
 * One component, not the library: this is a deep import through the package's
 * `./components/*` export, and `theme.ts:82` self-registers when
 * `window.alAutoRegistry` is true — which Shell.astro sets inline in <head> on
 * every page, live or not (.altitude/REGISTRATION.md).
 *
 * `<al-layout>` rides along for the same reason (spec
 * 2026-08-28-southleft-docs-parity-with-example-site, R4): the docs pages
 * arrange their sections with the design system's own layout primitive
 * instead of hand-rolled grids, and a page with no live components still has
 * to upgrade those. Two deep imports, still not the library — and the boot
 * blur in Shell.astro waits on both, so the moment the grids snap into place
 * is covered by the same blur that covers the token re-resolution.
 */
---

<script>
  import '@southleft/al-web-components/components/theme';
  import '@southleft/al-web-components/components/layout';
</script>
